// Change: new rule
// Title: HackTool - Certsync Execution
// Sigma ID: 745f66fc-ad78-43a7-807b-58cba1afb7e4
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1649, T1003.006
// Description: Detects execution of certsync, a tool that abuses Active Directory Certificate Services to
//   synchronise all domain hashes. It performs a Golden Certificate attack by requesting a
//   certificate for every domain user and recovering their NT hashes via UnPAC-the-Hash, effectively
//   replicating the impact of DCSync without using the replication RPC interface.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/zblurx/certsync
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6b9ade7935a13d35a57e75ff2587fbedcc53ef56/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_certsync.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\certsync" or ((FolderPath contains "\\python" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName contains "python") and ProcessCommandLine contains "certsync")
